//? Title: Finite differences: from a boundary-value problem to a checked tridiagonal solve
//? Subtitle: Actual source samples, boundary elimination, discrete residuals and second-order nodal error
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given a source f and endpoint values, reconstruct u on the unit interval from −u''=f.
The unknown is a function, so a numerical solver must choose both a finite representation
and a way to measure its error. A uniform central-difference stencil gives a tridiagonal
system solved in linear work by the native Thomas solver. This report starts with one
unknown, inspects actual assembly with nonzero boundaries, retains the original sine
refinements, and separates a small discrete residual from error in the continuous solution.
)

\toc

> The method: sample, eliminate the boundaries, solve

Let n be the number of interior points, h=1/(n+1), and x_i=ih. With U_0=α and U_{n+1}=β,
the three-point approximation is

$$
\frac{-U_{i-1}+2U_i-U_{i+1}}{h^2}=f(x_i),\qquad 1\le i\le n.
$$
\alttext(The negative second derivative is approximated by minus the left value, plus twice the centre value, minus the right value, all divided by the squared spacing.)

The interior matrix has diagonal 2/h² and off-diagonals −1/h². Move the known endpoint
terms to the RHS with positive signs: add α/h² to its first entry, then β/h² to its last.
When n=1, both additions belong to the same equation. The native result retains the
source samples before these additions and the assembled RHS after them.

For an interior vector v extended by zero endpoints,

$$
v^T A v=\frac1{h^2}\sum_{i=0}^{n}(v_{i+1}-v_i)^2>0\quad(v\ne0).
$$
\alttext(The quadratic form equals the sum of squared neighbour differences divided by the squared spacing, and is positive for any nonzero interior vector.)

Thus the matrix is symmetric positive definite. Its special tridiagonal structure
permits Thomas elimination without pivoting. Forward elimination removes one sub-diagonal
entry per row; backward substitution recovers one unknown per row. Both work and storage
are O(n), in addition to the n source-callback evaluations. This says nothing about their
individual costs or the runtime of a dense general solver.

> One unknown: eight times the midpoint value equals one

Take f=1, zero endpoints and n=1. The spacing is 1/2, so the sole equation is
8U_1=1 and U_1=1/8. The exact solution x(1−x)/2 has the same three nodal values.
If we join the numerical nodes by straight segments, the value at x=1/4 is 1/16,
whereas the exact quadratic is 3/32. Nodal exactness does not make a straight-line
representation exact between the nodes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fd_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
#include <climits>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
const auto r=dm::algorithms::finite_difference_poisson_solve([](double){return 1.;},0,0,1);
  const double joined=dm::algorithms::linear_interpolate(r.x,r.u,.25),exact=.25*.75/2;
  std::print("| node | x | native U |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<r.x.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n",i,r.x[i],r.u[i]);
  std::print("\nActual diagonal {}; off-diagonal {}; RHS {}; discrete residual {}.\n",r.diagonal,r.off_diagonal,r.rhs[0],r.max_abs_residual);
  std::print("At x=0.25: joined nodes {}; exact {}; absolute error {}.\n",joined,exact,std::abs(joined-exact));
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(62,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle b;b.width=3.1;b.height=1.6;b.font_size=24;
  g.node("left",{0,0},"x = 0\nU = 0",b).node("mid",{5,0},std::format("x = 1/2\nU = {}",r.u[1]),b).node("right",{10,0},"x = 1\nU = 0",b).edge("left","mid","weight -4").edge("right","mid","weight -4");
  g.text({5,2.6},"A source sample becomes one equation",28).text({5,-2.3},std::format("{} × U(midpoint) = {}",r.diagonal,r.rhs[0]),29).text({5,-3.7},"Exact at the nodes; interpolation still has error",24).save_svg("build/fd_tiny.svg");
  if(r.u[1]!=.125||std::abs(joined-exact)!=.03125)throw std::runtime_error("tiny identity");
}
