> Three unknowns: inspect the actual boundary contributions

Use f=1, α=2, β=5 and n=3. Then h=1/4 and the actual system is

$$
\begin{pmatrix}32&-16&0\\-16&32&-16\\0&-16&32\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}U_1\\U_2\\U_3\end{pmatrix}
=\begin{pmatrix}33\\1\\81\end{pmatrix}.
$$
\alttext(The three by three matrix has thirty-two on the diagonal and minus sixteen next to it. The right-hand side is thirty-three, one and eighty-one.)

The first RHS is 1+16×2=33; the last is 1+16×5=81. Elimination gives pivots
32,24,64/3. Substitution yields 91/32,29/8,139/32. The program reads the actual
source, RHS and residual from the native result; it does not reassemble or solve
the system in the report. Its exact reference is 2+3x+x(1−x)/2.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fd_boundaries.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
