> Why second order is conditional

For an exact solution with bounded continuous fourth derivative, Taylor expansion gives
an O(h²) truncation error. A discrete maximum-principle barrier w_i=x_i(1−x_i)/2
satisfies Aw=1 and max w_i≤1/8. It gives the exact-arithmetic inverse bound
||A^{-1}||∞≤1/8, and therefore

$$
\max_i |U_i-u(x_i)|\le\frac{h^2}{96}\max_{x\in[0,1]}|u^{(4)}(x)|.
$$
\alttext(The maximum nodal error is at most the squared spacing times the largest absolute fourth derivative, divided by ninety-six, for the exact discrete solve.)

This bound concerns the exact solution of the discrete equations with exact source samples.
Floating-point assembly and solution add their own errors. A recomputed residual r=AÛ−d
instead bounds distance to the exact solution of that assembled discrete system by
||Û−U||∞≤||r||∞/8 in exact residual arithmetic. A small residual is not a bound on the
truncation error. The native residual uses the stored binary64 matrix and RHS, evaluates
products and sums in long double, then stores rounded doubles. It is a diagnostic,
not a certified interval bound.

The stencil samples f only at the interior nodes. No generic second-order promise applies
to arbitrary discontinuous forcing, unresolved features, nonsmooth solutions or input
callbacks whose samples are already inaccurate. Joining nodes requires a separate
representation; linear interpolation adds its own O(h²) error when u has bounded second
derivative. This report uses no external dataset because manufactured solutions provide
exact controls for those distinct claims.

> Preserve the original sine profile and refinements

Keep −u''=π²sin(πx), zero endpoints, n=19 for the profile and the original n=9,19,39,79,159
refinements. Each grid includes its midpoint. On these grids the sampled sine is an
eigenvector with eigenvalue λ_h=4sin²(πh/2)/h². Thus the exact discrete solution is
(π²/λ_h)sin(πx_i), and the maximum nodal error is π²/λ_h−1. This supplies an independent
analytical prediction for the measured error and its limiting h² coefficient π²/12.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/fd_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
#include <climits>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
constexpr double pi=std::numbers::pi_v<double>;
  const auto f=[](double x){return pi*pi*std::sin(pi*x);};
  const auto r=dm::algorithms::finite_difference_poisson_solve(f,0,0,19);
  std::vector<double>x,y;for(int i=0;i<=200;++i){const double t=i/200.;x.push_back(t);y.push_back(std::sin(pi*t));}
  std::print("| n | h | maximum nodal error | eigenmode prediction | previous/current | discrete residual |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  std::vector<double>lh,le,guide;double previous=0;
  for(int n:{9,19,39,79,159}){
    const auto s=dm::algorithms::finite_difference_poisson_solve(f,0,0,n);
    const auto e=dm::algorithms::interpolation_error_scan([&](double t){return dm::algorithms::linear_interpolate(s.x,s.u,t);},[](double t){return std::sin(pi*t);},s.x);
    const double lambda=4*std::pow(std::sin(pi*s.h/2),2)/(s.h*s.h),predicted=pi*pi/lambda-1;
    std::print("| {} | {:.6f} | {:.3e} | {:.3e} | {:.6f} | {:.3e} |\n",n,s.h,e.max_abs_error,predicted,previous?previous/e.max_abs_error:0,s.max_abs_residual);
    lh.push_back(std::log10(s.h));le.push_back(std::log10(e.max_abs_error));guide.push_back(std::log10(pi*pi*s.h*s.h/12));previous=e.max_abs_error;
    if(std::abs(e.max_abs_error-predicted)>2e-11)throw std::runtime_error("sine eigenmode check");
  }
  auto profile=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();profile.line(x,y,"Exact sine",{16,185,129},2).points(r.x,r.u,"Native n=19",{220,38,38},5).title("Original sine profile").x_label("x").y_label("u(x)").y_limits(-.03,1.25).legend({"Exact sine","Native nodes, n=19"},{{16,185,129},{220,38,38}});
  auto error=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();error.line(lh,le,"Measured",{37,99,235},2).points(lh,le,"",{37,99,235},5).line(lh,guide,"Asymptotic h²",{148,163,184},1.5).title("Original five-grid convergence").x_label("log10 h").y_label("log10 maximum nodal error");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(profile).add(error).size(1100,540).title("Sine: profile agreement and measured second order").fit_panels().save_svg("build/fd_original.svg");
}
```
